description:
Build `ProbeSet`, a set of `std::uint64_t` values stored with **linear probing** in a power-of-two table:

```cpp
class ProbeSet
{
public:
    ProbeSet();                                // capacity 8
    bool insert(std::uint64_t key);            // true if it was not there
    bool contains(std::uint64_t key) const;
    bool erase(std::uint64_t key);             // true if it was there
    std::size_t size() const;
    std::size_t capacity() const;
    std::size_t tombstones() const;
};
```

- Each slot is **empty**, **full** (holding a key) or a **tombstone** (a key was erased).
- The home slot of a key is `mix(key) & (capacity - 1)`, with `mix` the SplitMix64 finaliser from lesson 2.04 (it is in the starter). Probe forward one slot at a time, wrapping around.
- `contains` and `erase` probe until they find the key or an **empty** slot; they skip over tombstones. `erase` turns the slot into a tombstone.
- `insert` first checks whether the key is present. If not, it places the key in the **first tombstone or empty slot** it passed on that probe.
- Before an insertion that would make `size + tombstones` exceed **3/4** of the capacity, rebuild the table: to **double** the capacity if `size + 1` would exceed half of it, otherwise at the same capacity. A rebuild reinserts every key and drops every tombstone.

